# Secrets shared by every deploy destination (staging, production, and
# destination-less `kamal deploy`). Kamal loads `.kamal/secrets-common` first,
# then `.kamal/secrets.<destination>` (or `.kamal/secrets` when no destination
# is given), so anything defined here is available everywhere.
#
# Secrets defined here are available for reference under registry/password,
# env/secret, builder/secrets, and accessories/*/env/secret in config/deploy.yml.
# All secrets must be pulled from a password manager, ENV, or a file.
# DO NOT ENTER RAW CREDENTIALS HERE! This file needs to be safe for git.

# Grab the registry password from ENV. In GitHub Actions this comes from the
# KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD repository secret.
KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD

# Read locally from config/master.key. CI writes that file from the
# RAILS_MASTER_KEY secret before invoking Kamal. Never check config/master.key
# into git.
RAILS_MASTER_KEY=$(cat config/master.key)
